--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Captured 2 September 2026 from qemu-system-xtensa 9.0.0 (esp-develop), -M esp32s3 -m 4M,
against the sdkconfig.defaults + sdkconfig.phase1 + sdkconfig.qemu build.

THIS IS AN EMULATOR, NOT A UNIT.  QEMU's esp32s3 machine has no octal PSRAM, no microSD,
no ES8388 and no ADS1299, so every peripheral this firmware talks to is absent.  What the
run proves is the part that does not need them: the image boots, the bootloader reads THIS
partition table, the app is loaded from the factory slot, app_main() runs, and the three
driver bring-up paths behave as they were written to.  What it proves nothing about is any
register value, daisy-chain order or SPI timing, because there is no silicon to disagree.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Re-captured 2 September 2026 after FW-D17 and FW-D18, to show that reworking the contact
light driver did not disturb the boot path.  The run reaches the same place as before and
stops the same way: the 6 MiB sample ring will not allocate, because CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT
asks for octal PSRAM and QEMU has none, so app_main() calls abort() and the chip reboots
into the loop this file's own header calls out.  That is the open PSRAM failure mode, not a
new fault.

Nothing here exercises the lights.  lights_task() alternates two lead-off comparator
thresholds over SPI and drives a 74HC595; QEMU has neither an ADS1299 to answer nor an LED
to light, and the task never starts because app_main() aborts before it is created.  E-27
remains what it was: met in the source, never seen.
